{"uid":"4afe1f0cd779eece","name":"test_refuted_entries_are_persisted_but_never_exempt","fullName":"tests.test_petition_adjudications_run_scope#test_refuted_entries_are_persisted_but_never_exempt","historyId":"4f1575de96bc9fcb703e8c18d795c84b","time":{"start":1791941882301,"stop":1791941882309,"duration":8},"description":"Task 016 (approach 02, review finding 2) changed the product here:\n    `record_confirmed_adjudications` now persists REFUTED entries too --\n    same store, same keyed MAC -- because that store is what\n    `run_record.build_petitions_section` renders, and a REFUTED\n    adjudication and its remedy were otherwise lost to the run record.\n    What must NOT change (and is pinned here) is the EXEMPTION rule: the\n    exemption readers (`read_confirmed_adjudications`,\n    `confirmed_obligations`) still see CONFIRMED entries only, so a\n    REFUTED entry in the store exempts nothing. This test previously\n    asserted the file was never written at all; that expectation was the\n    render bug, not the property.\n\n    #209 §5 adds the third reader and the distinction that makes it safe:\n    `settled_obligations` sees BOTH verdicts, because it answers \"has review\n    already ruled on this at all\" for the one purpose of not re-presenting a\n    settled obligation to a later review pass. The tail of this node pins\n    SETTLED growing while EXEMPT does not -- the exact property that would\n    be violated if a later change pointed an exemption reader at the wider\n    set. Every assertion above is unchanged and none is relaxed.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 016 (approach 02, review finding 2) changed the product here:<br />\n<code>record_confirmed_adjudications</code> now persists REFUTED entries too --<br />\nsame store, same keyed MAC -- because that store is what<br />\n<code>run_record.build_petitions_section</code> renders, and a REFUTED<br />\nadjudication and its remedy were otherwise lost to the run record.<br />\nWhat must NOT change (and is pinned here) is the EXEMPTION rule: the<br />\nexemption readers (<code>read_confirmed_adjudications</code>,<br />\n<code>confirmed_obligations</code>) still see CONFIRMED entries only, so a<br />\nREFUTED entry in the store exempts nothing. This test previously<br />\nasserted the file was never written at all; that expectation was the<br />\nrender bug, not the property.</p>\n<pre><code>#209 §5 adds the third reader and the distinction that makes it safe:\n`settled_obligations` sees BOTH verdicts, because it answers &quot;has review\nalready ruled on this at all&quot; for the one purpose of not re-presenting a\nsettled obligation to a later review pass. The tail of this node pins\nSETTLED growing while EXEMPT does not -- the exact property that would\nbe violated if a later change pointed an exemption reader at the wider\nset. Every assertion above is unchanged and none is relaxed.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791941650409,"stop":1791941650410,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791941650410,"stop":1791941650410,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791941882283,"stop":1791941882283,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791941882283,"stop":1791941882288,"duration":5},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"par